WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.960
What if Penny was hiding a deep, dark secret&nbsp;
from the guys since the very first episode? Too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.320
hard to believe? Well keep watching, because we’re&nbsp;
diving into a fan theory that changes everything.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.440
If you really think about it, we barely know&nbsp;
anything about The Big Bang Theory's Penny who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:23.520
until she marries Leonard in season 9, doesn't&nbsp;
even have a last name. She's beautiful and blonde,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.800
but that doesn't mean her supposed acting career&nbsp;
is going anywhere. She can somehow afford to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.240
in the same apartment building as several working&nbsp;
scientists in spite of her waitress' salary.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.200
"You realize, Penny, that the&nbsp;
technology that went into this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.040
arm will one day make unskilled food&nbsp;
servers such as yourself obsolete."

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.040
"Really? They're going to make a&nbsp;
robot that spits on your hamburger?"

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.240
All the while, her character seems to have nothing&nbsp;
at all in common with Leonard and his friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.600
Yet she still spends almost all&nbsp;
of her time hanging out with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.120
eating Chinese food, and listening to them nerd&nbsp;
out about subjects she doesn't seem to grasp.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.800
It speaks to a crisis in the very&nbsp;
foundation of the show's premise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.560
that these inconsistencies are never probed, let&nbsp;
alone explained. Look too hard at the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.280
Penny, and based on the sheer improbability&nbsp;
of this one woman's choices and traits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.200
you'll see all the cracks that should have&nbsp;
brought the entire structure of the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.640
crumbling down. Fortunately, there's a&nbsp;
fan theory that provides an explanation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.400
for all of these apparent plot holes, and its&nbsp;
implications are pretty darn wild to comprehend.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.760
According to this fan theory,&nbsp;
first posited by Reddit user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.160
numbertheory and picked up by Screen&nbsp;
Rant, it's quite possible that Penny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:42.400
is secretly a spy. That's right — move over The&nbsp;
Americans, because Chuck Lorre's got an entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.120
different story to tell about a deep-cover&nbsp;
agent living among her unsuspecting marks.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.880
The theory ties into the notion that the federal&nbsp;
government has been spying on Sheldon and Leonard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.080
ever since the latter broke up with Joyce Kim —&nbsp;
a woman who was revealed to be a North Korean spy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.160
in the episode The Staircase Implementation. An&nbsp;
upset Leonard causes an explosion that takes out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.360
the building's elevators, which may not interest&nbsp;
local authorities for very long but — coupled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.160
with the Kim incident — very well could have&nbsp;
drawn the attention of the federal government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.840
Aware of Leonard and Sheldon's&nbsp;
knowledge of a rocket fuel project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.320
they simply sent Penny in to monitor&nbsp;
both men, according to the theory.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.840
It sounds absurd, but it actually ties up all&nbsp;
of the lingering confusion about her lifestyle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.640
Think about it: Penny, without even an&nbsp;
identifiable last name, has been sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:38.240
into the men's lives to observe their antics. This&nbsp;
explains why she spends so much time with two guys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.040
who don't share her interests, why she doesn’t&nbsp;
have any friends of her own, how she can afford&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.720
an apartment without a roommate, and why there's&nbsp;
a lack of traction in her so-called acting career.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.793
"When you were telling Kevin about your&nbsp;
acting career did you mention your long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.793 --> 00:02:56.640
running role as waitress in a local&nbsp;
production of The Cheesecake Factory?"

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.320
All obvious violations of Occam's razor&nbsp;
aside, sometimes it's the explanation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.200
actually explains everything that's worthy&nbsp;
of consideration — unlike the real-life Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.920
Bang Theory, ironically enough. You can&nbsp;
think of it as a Unified Theory of Penny.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.720
"No cops, be cool!"

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.720
If you're still having trouble wrapping your&nbsp;
head around the possibility that Penny is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:22.720
the spy next door, then consider this:&nbsp;
Despite Penny's lack of multiple PhDs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.400
The Big Bang Theory makes it clear&nbsp;
she's not an idiot — far from it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.800
in fact. Without the slow reveal of&nbsp;
Penny's intelligence over the course of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.840
long character arc, would her relationship with&nbsp;
the objectively brilliant Leonard even work?

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.480
Maybe — just maybe — she plays it all "babe in the&nbsp;
woods" whenever the boys descend into science talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.280
just to keep their guard down. Maybe&nbsp;
she feigns a total lack of understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.800
to lure this apartment full of useful idiots&nbsp;
into a false sense of security. If they knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.120
right from the get-go that Penny understood&nbsp;
even a fraction of what they were saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.760
maybe they would have been more guarded with the&nbsp;
details of their work. Her performative ignorance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:06.720
provides them with just the level of comfort they&nbsp;
need to spill each and every classified bean.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:12.480
All the while, if this theory is to be believed&nbsp;
at least, Penny could be carefully recording&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.160
any and all information that may be&nbsp;
of interest to federal intelligence.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.880
Now go back and watch the entire series from&nbsp;
the beginning with this new understanding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.560
It's a totally different show.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.120
"That's about it. That's the story of Penny."

